## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a simple, scalable ingestion path with clear isolation and observable state using familiar GCP primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming ingestion
- Cloud Run consumer with auto-scaling
- Idempotent processing via Pub/Sub message_id and an idempotence store
- Per-tenant isolation using separate BigQuery datasets
- Least-privilege IAM, Cloud Logging/Monitoring
- Basic test plan with replay and failure injection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-handler showing idempotent check
async function handle(msg) {
  const id = msg.message_id;
  if (await isProcessed(id)) return;
  await enrichAndStore(msg);
  await markProcessed(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle backpressure if tenants spike?
- What changes to support a new tenant without code redeployments?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time ingestion basics, per-tenant routing, idempotence, and basic observability on GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming sources; Dataflow (Python) transforms
- BigQuery per-tenant tables with environmental isolation
- Idempotence via insertId; dead-letter queue handling
- Basic monitoring and dashboards for latency/cost

## Code Example
```javascript
class ValidateAndRoute {
  process(element) {
    const data = JSON.parse(element);
    if (!data.tenant_id || !data.timestamp || data.value == null) return;
    return [{ tenant: data.tenant_id, value: data.value }];
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test DLQ routing and failed-event replay?
- What metrics would you surface in a simple dashboard to catch data skew or lag?
